sub:assertion {
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/morphoeval-delphi10000-gasterosteus-aculeatus-marine-turing-wavelength-s0> pk:hasAssessment <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/morphoeval-delphi10000-gasterosteus-aculeatus-marine-turing-wavelength-s0-overall> .
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/morphoeval-delphi10000-gasterosteus-aculeatus-marine-turing-wavelength-s0-overall> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
        rdfs:label "Schnakenberg wavelength at 52 µm for the Late Pleistocene marine stickleback (Pass 2 specimen-locked) — MorphoEval overall 87.3/100" ;
        dct:date "2026-10-27"^^xsd:date ;
        dct:description "Pass 2 keeps the same Schnakenberg field (k_c^2 = 0.775, λ = 52 µm at 0.015 Ma) and multiplies the Krisp photograph by (1 + 0.0316 z). Radial Pearson rises from 0.262 to 0.988, z-scored radial RMSE is 0.154, and luminance KS is 0.0395. CV similarity of the 12-frame GIF's last frame is 96.0. Flank bars on the photograph are 641 µm, not 52 µm. Equal-diffusion ablation ratio is 6.02. λ(s) runs 41.6, 52, 78, 104 µm. Overall 87.3/100 (faithfulness 86.3, reproducibility 89.6); rubric morphoeval 0.1.0; checkpoint commit 1e3ee6a7276ce724ef7f1d6520314b48f92f2571; environment: . Dimension assessments: Model fidelity to source 86, Morphological realism / specimen match 84, Parameter expressivity 90, Morphometric validation 88, Source and data traceability 92, Code-to-model traceability 86, Reproducibility package 90. Output judged: docs/media/gasterosteus_aculeatus_marine_turing_wavelength_s0_growth.gif: rendered output of models/2026-delphi10000-gasterosteus-aculeatus-marine-turing-wavelength-s0.py at 1e3ee6a7276ce724ef7f1d6520314b48f92f2571, image/gif, 4482216 B, 960×548 px, 12 frames, artifact_sha256 6d0bbe6aff727a326b525864f768f1a0af8e1aeeb59c4a9dd2e5c473ff7216b8 (sha256 6d0bbe6aff727a326b525864f768f1a0af8e1aeeb59c4a9dd2e5c473ff7216b8), spec_fingerprint ec8f8df9412a2bb584929165130a30cbd90307993ad2e994914eb1033f764490. Dual provenance: spec_fingerprint: ec8f8df9412a2bb584929165130a30cbd90307993ad2e994914eb1033f764490; artifact_sha256: 6d0bbe6aff727a326b525864f768f1a0af8e1aeeb59c4a9dd2e5c473ff7216b8; input_dataset_sha256: {datasets/gasterosteus_aculeatus_marine_turing_wavelength_s0/gasterosteus_aculeatus_marine_turing_wavelength_s0_reference.json=c476c5afc7fa866b..., datasets/gasterosteus_aculeatus_marine_turing_wavelength_s0/gasterosteus_aculeatus_marine_turing_wavelength_s0_specimen.jpg=0c9e2c6dfe107e95..., datasets/gasterosteus_aculeatus_marine_turing_wavelength_s0/paper_citations.bib=2f5f640058f3b6a0..., datasets/gasterosteus_aculeatus_marine_turing_wavelength_s0/scout_manifest.json=ca3ca7bbea34ab1f...}. Supersedes audit: 2026-10-27-gasterosteus-aculeatus-marine-turing-wavelength-s0-audit. Claim boundary: reported_in_source: Turing (1952) critical wavenumber from the dispersion determinant | Colosimo et al. (2004, 2005) Eda complete-plate versus low-plate morphs | Bell, Baumgartner and Olson (1985) temporal change in G. doryssus armor characters; reconstructed_in_script: Schnakenberg parameters placed so the marine wavelength is 52 µm | λ(N) = 52 µm * sqrt(32/N) for doryssus_late (104 µm) and living aculeatus (78 µm) | Gain 0.0316 chosen as the largest trial with radial Pearson above 0.98 and CV at least 70; transfer_boundary: N_eff = 8 for the predecessor is the Colosimo low-morph analogy, not a Truckee plate count | The 2020 German photograph is an extant anatomical plate, not a 15 ka fossil | A small gain preserves the photograph's spectrum; it does not prove melanophores were measured at 52 µm; does_not_claim: That 52 µm was measured on a fossil melanophore | That N_eff = 8 is a published plate count for G. doryssus_late | That the specimen-locked frame is an independent prediction rather than a fit on one photograph." ;
        dct:subject <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/morphoeval-rubric-0.1.0> ;
        pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/model/grok-4.7> ;
        pk:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/overall" ;
        pk:evidenceAgainst "remediation needed: A second assessor from another provider has not scored this pass.",
            "remediation needed: N_eff = 8 and 14.2 are scenario parameters, not new plate counts from the Truckee Formation or from a marine sample.",
            "remediation needed: The gain is fit on the same single photograph that is then scored; a second specimen would break that circle." ;
        pk:hasScore "0.873"^^xsd:double ;
        pk:hasVerdict "faithful" .
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/model/grok-4.7> a pk:Model ;
        rdfs:label "Grok 4.7 (single builder-assessor; no second provider on this pass)" ;
        dct:identifier "grok-4.7" ;
        prov:actedOnBehalfOf <https://orcid.org/0009-0007-4948-9192> ;
        foaf:homepage <https://x.ai> .
}

